                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.112 Er 4/3.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Minister in
                        temporary charge of the Embassy at Constantinople.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-11-28"><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The embassy is instructed to report what action has been taken on Department’s
                    telegram of November 1, 1910, also to investigate the reported arrest of
                    Erickson at Monastir on the 20th ultimo and to take appropriate action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
